SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Attention Trading Partners: Take Action Now B
 efore MaineCare’s New Online Portal Goes Live
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Attention Trading Partners: Take Action Now Before Main
 eCare’s New Online Portal Goes Live\nAttention Trading Partners: Take Ac
 tion Now Before MaineCare’s New Online Portal Goes Live\nAug 17\, 2026\n
 A refreshed and upgraded MIHMS is coming in mid October 2026. The Office o
 f MaineCare Services (OMS)\, in partnership with Gainwell Technologies\, i
 s launching an upgraded MIHMS\, to bring enhanced security\, improved usab
 ility\, and a more modern experience to better support your day-to-day wor
 k.\nThe upgrade will include a new “MaineCare Partner Portal” that wil
 l replace what is known today as the “Health PAS Online Portal.” Pleas
 e note that\, until the October go-live\, we will continue using the name 
 “Health PAS Online Portal” in communications related to current functi
 onality.\nYou can read more about the benefits to providers and members on
  the\nHealth PAS Online Portal\n.\nTrading Partners Preparation\nThis mess
 age is part of a series about changes to how trading partners will access 
 the new portal and what you must do now to prepare for these changes.\nTra
 ding partners include providers\, billing agents\, health plans\, clearing
 houses\, and business associates. Trading partners have an important role 
 to play in supporting a smooth transition and uninterrupted access to the 
 portal after go-live.\nPortal Access Impacts and Required Actions Before G
 o‑Live\nThe preparation activities and changes below will improve system
  security by ensuring the right people have the right access\, at go-live 
 and ongoing. Most actions are only for Admin (R7) users.\nMost important:\
 nProviders with duplicate emails need to make changes to their portal user
  accounts\nnow\nto assist with account migration to the upgraded portal.\n
 On September 1\, we will terminate current Admin (R7) user accounts that s
 hare an email address with another user account.\nWe will not terminate Ad
 min (R7) us\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/a
 ttention-trading-partners-take-action-now-mainecares-new-online-portal-goe
 s-live-2026-08-0
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/attention-
 trading-partners-take-action-now-mainecares-new-online-portal-goes-live-20
 26-08-0
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
